            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0556" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1504.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mexican
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In further reply to Mr. Pereyra’s
                    note of March 26 last, quoting a report from the governor of Sonora that armed
                    bands were invading that State from its northern boundary, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith a copy of a letter from the Attorney General, transmitting one
                    from the United States attorney for Arizona in relation to the matter.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d684-a1.xml" xpointer="d684-a1"/>
            </div>
